    "source_issues": [
      "Exam e006 reads 'Heart: Respiratory rate and rhythm', evidently a mis-expansion of 'RRR' (regular rate and rhythm); recorded as regular rate and rhythm with the original wording in finding_flags (x011).",
      "The note lists 'Medications: Ibuprofen, aspirin', but the script's medication answer (p028) is 'Ibuprofen' only; aspirin appears only as a relieving factor (p014, f016).",
      "Note HPI says the pain is 'sometimes accompanied by nausea and vomiting'; the script says she vomited for the first time yesterday.",
      "p024 asks about joint pains and fatigue; the answer ('Occasional aches and pains treated with ibuprofen') does not address fatigue.",
      "Gold #2 cites 'Chronic headaches', but the script gives a 2-week history plus one similar headache in college.",
      "The patient name 'Kindly Clark' may be a transcription error; kept as given (the sample closure addresses 'Mrs. Clark'). The sample closure ends with a stray '[276]'."
    ],
    "notes": [
      "The parenthetical in p005 '(two to three times a day)' is content, not a stage direction; it is kept in f006. '(indicates the right side of the head)' in p007 is moved to extras.acting_notes.",
      "Temporality: the episodic pattern (intermittent, frequency, per-episode severity and duration, functional limitation during episodes, nausea during pain) is 'recurrent'; the headache present now (p012) is 'current'.",
      "Tubal ligation from p030 and p038 combined into one fact (f038); p038's denial of birth-control pills is a separate fact (f041).",
      "Following the worked example, the sp_notes direction 'look as if you are in severe pain' is kept as an acting note only; the note exam (x005) already records severe pain.",
      "The patient description 'married with three children' exists only in raw_opening; kept in extras.acting_notes (p036 also gives husband and three children).",
      "Conversion: p012 'I currently have one' (v1 f014) is merged into the chief-complaint fact f001 ('I have a headache. I have one right now.'), since a separate 'headache right now' fact would paraphrase the opening complaint; the time-of-day pattern stays a timing child (f014).",
      "Conversion: v1's three relieving facts (dark quiet room, sleep, aspirin) and three aggravating facts (stress, light, noise) become one relieving (f016) and one aggravating (f017) child with complete value lists, as in the reference conversion. Aura, timing, menses relationship, waking from sleep and the effect on work (v1 'functional') are children of the headache.",
      "Conversion: vomiting (p016) is split into the symptom (f020) and its onset child (f021); the earlier college headache (p022) is a parent with an 'other symptoms' child (f035); the sinusitis comparison is a child of the sinusitis fact (f037); last month's setback at work is a context child (f050) of the current work stress (f049).",
      "Conversion: birth control pills (f041; v1 subtype ob_gyn) are given category 'medication', following the schema ('medication: ... contraception'), although the CONVERSION.md subtype table maps ob_gyn to medical_history.",
      "Conversion: the note's 'VS: Within normal limits' (e002) agrees with the doorway values and is cited on each doorway vital record. The HEENT line (e003) is split into head, eye, and nose-and-throat records.",
      "Harmonisation pass: scale [0, 10] added to f007.",
      "Fixes: f011 answer word removed; f013 answer word removed; f015 answer word removed; f018 answer word removed; f020 answer word removed; f022 answer word removed; f028 answer word removed; f029 answer word removed; f030 answer word removed; f031 answer word removed; f033 answer word removed; f034 answer word removed; f041 answer word removed; f042 answer word removed; f049 answer word removed."
    ],
